04:54.268 --> 05:00.934
[SPEAKER_00]: And so I mentioned a few things about that before, like the need of putting, mostly trying to rely on

05:17.627 --> 05:24.234
[SPEAKER_01]: sort of authentic elder teacher who are beyond any doubt so that one's faith will be always put in the right place.

05:24.775 --> 05:35.707
[SPEAKER_01]: But in any case, before relying to any teacher, first we should examine or think about the teacher from the distance, hear about his life or what he or she does.

05:36.487 --> 05:49.854
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, on closer by, I can see if that teacher lives and teaches and behaves and is in accordance with what are the qualifications of a true, genuine teacher.

05:50.755 --> 06:02.501
[SPEAKER_01]: And if one finds, given little time for that, that the teacher is really authentic, as described in the scriptures, and then one can rely upon that teacher.

06:03.421 --> 06:28.380
[SPEAKER_01]: once one has rely upon that teacher then it is important to trust whatever advice and guidance the teacher will give because that kind of confidence is very important so that one travels the path without sort of all the time doubts and hesitations and sort of double mind and things like that and so that is crucial

